  # ─── Strategic-Oya disciplines (v0.3+) ─────────────────────────────────
  #
  # These rules are triggered by the scope sensor at slice-claim — not by
  # agent citation in comms. When the sensor fires on a slice, Oya posts an
  # @OYA Recommendation naming the discipline; the pair either produces the
  # required artefact in the planning doc (catch) or acknowledges and proceeds
  # (skipped). Forgiving authority — never blocks the slice.
  #
  # Each rule has a `skipped` counter in addition to fires/catches/bypasses.
  # Skip patterns are tracked but not enforced; they surface at cycle close
  # as operator-facing signals.

  - id: threat-model-auth-changes
    type: strategic-discipline
    scope: framework
    runbook_section: "AGENT_COLLAB_RUNBOOK.md § Strategic disciplines § Threat-model auth changes"
    citation_pattern: "threat-model-auth-changes"
    provenance:
      added_in_runbook_version: "1.8"
      added_on: 2026-05-20
      added_reason: |
        First strategic-Oya discipline. Triggered by scope sensor when a slice's
        touched files or planning doc indicates auth-surface changes (sessions,
        tokens, identity provider config, OAuth/OIDC/SAML, authentication
        boundary modifications). Required artefact: STRIDE table in the
        planning doc covering spoofing / tampering / repudiation /
        info-disclosure / DoS / elevation-of-privilege.

        Tool-choice is operator-side — gstack /cso, raw prompting, OWASP
        checklist, vendor skill: musubi tracks the artefact, not the tool.
        Forgiving authority: pair can skip with acknowledgement; skip is
        logged and surfaced at cycle close.
    fires: { total: 0, by_cycle: {} }
    catches: { total: 0, by_class: {}, examples: [] }
    bypasses: { total: 0, examples: [] }
    skipped: { total: 0, examples: [] }
    silent_misses: { total: 0, examples: [] }
    notes: |
      Sensor implementation: scripts/classify-slice-disciplines.py.
      Trigger patterns: path matches /auth/ /sessions/ /tokens/ /oauth/
      /oidc/ /saml/ /iam/ /password/ /identity-provider/; content matches
      authentication, authorization, session/access/refresh token, auth
      boundary. Refine the sensor's pattern list (not this rule's name)
      if false positives or negatives accumulate.

